Project Overview: Neurotransmitter Simulation
This is an interactive 3D visualization project that simulates neurotransmitter behavior at the synaptic level, built using Three.js. The simulation aims to provide an educational tool for understanding neural signaling.

Key Components:
Synaptic Structure
Detailed presynaptic terminal with bulbous shape
Anatomically accurate synaptic cleft (20-40nm spacing)
Postsynaptic membrane with receptor clusters
Voltage-gated calcium channels
Synaptic vesicles with neurotransmitters

Neurotransmitter Types:
Dopamine
Serotonin
Glutamate
GABA
Norepinephrine
Each with unique properties (color, release rate, reuptake rate, diffusion speed)

Interactive Features
Release neurotransmitter buttons
Neurotransmitter type selection
Reset functionality
Camera controls for viewing different angles
Real-time visualization of neurotransmitter effects

Biological Processes Simulated
Action potential arrival
Calcium channel activation
Vesicle release
Neurotransmitter diffusion
Receptor binding
Reuptake mechanisms
Enzymatic degradation

Recent Improvements:
